Third-party notices
===================

sqlglot test suite
------------------

Case files under cases/imported/ whose `origin` field names sqlglot are derived from the test
suite of sqlglot (https://github.com/tobymao/sqlglot), file tests/dialects/test_snowflake.py.
Only the Snowflake SQL of each fixture is used as case input; SQLQuack records the expected
answer from Snowflake itself. sqlglot's expected DuckDB output is kept in the `sqlglot_duckdb`
field as reference side data only: it is never asserted, does not count toward verification and
is not part of the case hash.

The exact-check corpus corpora/polyglot-check/sqlglot.json holds the SQL of sqlglot's test
fixtures at v30.14.0 (tests/fixtures/identity.sql, tests/test_parser.py and tests/dialects/),
as extracted by polyglot's fixture tooling. polyglot, below, is itself inspired by sqlglot and
ships sqlglot's licence. corpora/polyglot-check/sqlglot_postgres.json holds the SQL of
tests/dialects/test_postgres.py at the same version, and corpora/polyglot-check/sqlglot_sqlite.json
that of tests/dialects/test_sqlite.py.

The referee corpus referee/corpora/sqlglot.json holds the query statements passed to
`validate_identity` and `validate_all` in tests/dialects/test_snowflake.py at the sqlglot commit
its `origin` field names. Only Snowflake's syntax verdict on each statement is recorded.

